IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division C, "Rulings and Appeals": sections 26.1 to 29. LAYER 1, from the text alone.
--
-- A person may ask an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency for a ruling on whether a job is pensionable, how
-- long it lasts, what the earnings and contributions are and who the employer is (section 26.1). A ruling can be
-- appealed to the Minister (section 27), as can an assessment of an employer (section 27.1); the Minister's decision
-- can be appealed to the Tax Court of Canada (section 28). Decisions are final and binding (section 29).
--
-- Every rule is constitutive. A time limit of "90 days after" is the keel's `a number of days` limit: the day
-- itself and the ninetieth day after it are both in time (fork F1). The date a decision is "communicated" is a plain
-- input, because subsection 28(1.1) leaves it to a rule of the Tax Court that is not deposited (fork F16).

§ `Division C -- Rulings and Appeals`

§§ `s 26.1 -- rulings`

-- "may request an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency authorized by the Minister of National Revenue to make a ruling
-- on any of the following questions".
-- src:731 | Request for ruling
-- src:732 | 26.1 (1) The Minister of Employment and Social Development, an employer, an employee or a person claiming to be an employer or an employee may request an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency authorized by the Minister of National Revenue to make a ruling on any of the following questions:
-- src:733 | (a) whether an employment is pensionable;
-- src:734 | (b) how long an employment lasts, including the dates on which it begins and ends;
-- src:735 | (c) what is the amount of any earnings from pensionable employment;
-- src:736 | (d) whether a contribution is payable;
-- src:737 | (e) what is the amount of a contribution that is payable; and
-- src:738 | (f) who is the employer of a person in pensionable employment.
@ref Act s 26.1(1) (src:731-738)
DECLARE `cp2 Kind of person requesting a ruling` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister of Employment and Social Development requesting a ruling`
    `an employer requesting a ruling`
    `an employee requesting a ruling`
    `a person claiming to be an employer requesting a ruling`
    `a person claiming to be an employee requesting a ruling`
    `another person requesting a ruling`

@ref Act s 26.1(1)(a) to (f) (src:731-738)
DECLARE `cp2 Question for a ruling` IS ONE OF
    `whether an employment is pensionable`
    `how long an employment lasts, including the dates on which it begins and ends`
    `what is the amount of any earnings from pensionable employment`
    `whether a contribution is payable`
    `what is the amount of a contribution that is payable`
    `who is the employer of a person in pensionable employment`
    `another question`

@ref Act s 26.1(1) (src:731-738)
GIVEN requester IS A `cp2 Kind of person requesting a ruling`
      question IS A `cp2 Question for a ruling`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26.1(1) — the person may request a ruling on the question` requester question MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF requester EQUALS `another person requesting a ruling` THEN FALSE
        IF question EQUALS `another question` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:739 | Time limit
-- src:740 | (2) The Minister of Employment and Social Development may request a ruling at any time, but a request by any other person must be made before June 30 of the year after the year in respect of which the question relates.
@ref Act s 26.1(2) (src:739-740)
GIVEN requester IS A `cp2 Kind of person requesting a ruling`
      `the year in respect of which the question relates` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the request is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26.1(2) — the request is made in time` requester `the year in respect of which the question relates` `the day the request is made` MEANS
    CONSIDER requester
    WHEN `the Minister of Employment and Social Development requesting a ruling` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `the day the request is made` LESS THAN (YMD (`the year in respect of which the question relates` PLUS 1) 6 30)

-- src:741 | Ruling
-- src:742 | (3) The authorized officer shall make the ruling within a reasonable time after receiving the request.
@ref Act s 26.1(3) (src:741-742)
GIVEN `the authorized officer received the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer made the ruling within a reasonable time after receiving the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26.1(3) — the authorized officer has made the ruling as required` `the authorized officer received the request` `the officer made the ruling within a reasonable time after receiving the request` MEANS
        `the authorized officer received the request`
    AND `the officer made the ruling within a reasonable time after receiving the request`

-- (4): "Unless a ruling has been requested with respect to a person in pensionable employment", what was deducted or
-- paid is deemed to have been deducted or paid in accordance with the Act, and what was not is deemed not to have
-- been required to be. Once a ruling is requested, neither presumption arises.
-- src:743 | Presumption
-- src:744 | (4) Unless a ruling has been requested with respect to a person in pensionable employment,
-- src:745 | (a) an amount deducted from the remuneration of the person or paid by an employer as a contribution for the person is deemed to have been deducted or paid in accordance with this Act; or
-- src:746 | (b) an amount that has not been so deducted or paid is deemed not to have been required to be deducted or paid in accordance with this Act.
@ref Act s 26.1(4) (src:743-746)
DECLARE `cp2 What the Act presumes about an amount` IS ONE OF
    `the amount is deemed to have been deducted or paid in accordance with this Act`
    `the amount is deemed not to have been required to be deducted or paid in accordance with this Act`
    `no presumption arises under subsection 26.1(4)`

@ref Act s 26.1(4) (src:743-746)
GIVEN `a ruling has been requested with respect to the person in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an amount has been deducted from the remuneration of the person, or paid by an employer as a contribution for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `cp2 What the Act presumes about an amount`
`s 26.1(4) — what the Act presumes about the amount` `a ruling has been requested with respect to the person in pensionable employment` `an amount has been deducted from the remuneration of the person, or paid by an employer as a contribution for the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a ruling has been requested with respect to the person in pensionable employment` THEN `no presumption arises under subsection 26.1(4)`
        IF `an amount has been deducted from the remuneration of the person, or paid by an employer as a contribution for the person` THEN `the amount is deemed to have been deducted or paid in accordance with this Act`
        OTHERWISE `the amount is deemed not to have been required to be deducted or paid in accordance with this Act`

§§ `s 27 to 27.3 -- appeals to the Minister`

-- src:747 | Appeal of rulings
-- src:748 | 27 An appeal to the Minister from a ruling may be made by the Minister of Employment and Social Development at any time, and by any other person concerned within 90 days after the person is notified of the ruling.
@ref Act s 27 (src:747-748)
GIVEN `the appeal is made by the Minister of Employment and Social Development` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is made by another person concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person was notified of the ruling` IS A DATE
      `the day of the appeal to the Minister` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27 — the appeal from the ruling is in time` `the appeal is made by the Minister of Employment and Social Development` `the appeal is made by another person concerned` `the day the person was notified of the ruling` `the day of the appeal to the Minister` MEANS
        `the appeal is made by the Minister of Employment and Social Development`
    OR  (    `the appeal is made by another person concerned`
         AND `a date is within a time limit after a start date`
                 `the day of the appeal to the Minister`
                 `the day the person was notified of the ruling`
                 (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90))

@ref Act s 27 (src:747-748)
GIVEN `the day the person was notified of the ruling` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 27 — the last day for a person concerned to appeal the ruling to the Minister` `the day the person was notified of the ruling` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the day the person was notified of the ruling` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90)

-- src:749 | Appeal of assessments
-- src:750 | 27.1 An employer who has been assessed under section 22 may appeal to the Minister for a reconsideration of the assessment, either as to whether an amount should be assessed as payable or as to the amount assessed, within 90 days after being notified of the assessment.
@ref Act s 27.1 (src:749-750)
GIVEN `the employer has been assessed under section 22` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the employer was notified of the assessment` IS A DATE
      `the day of the appeal to the Minister` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27.1 — the employer may appeal the assessment to the Minister for reconsideration` `the employer has been assessed under section 22` `the day the employer was notified of the assessment` `the day of the appeal to the Minister` MEANS
        `the employer has been assessed under section 22`
    AND `a date is within a time limit after a start date`
            `the day of the appeal to the Minister`
            `the day the employer was notified of the assessment`
            (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90)

@ref Act s 27.1 (src:749-750)
GIVEN `the day the employer was notified of the assessment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 27.1 — the last day for the employer to appeal the assessment to the Minister` `the day the employer was notified of the assessment` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the day the employer was notified of the assessment` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90)

-- src:751 | Notification of appeal
-- src:752 | 27.2 (1) Where an appeal is made to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1, the Minister shall
-- src:753 | (a) notify any person who may be affected by the appeal that the Minister intends to decide the appeal, including the Minister of Employment and Social Development in the case of an appeal of a ruling; and
-- src:754 | (b) give the person an opportunity to provide information and to make representations to protect the person’s interests, as the circumstances require.
@ref Act s 27.2(1) (src:751-754)
GIVEN `an appeal has been made to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person may be affected by the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27.2(1) — the Minister must notify the person and give the person an opportunity to provide information and make representations` `an appeal has been made to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1` `the person may be affected by the appeal` MEANS
        `an appeal has been made to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1`
    AND `the person may be affected by the appeal`

-- src:755 | Where appeal to be sent
-- src:756 | (2) An appeal shall be addressed to the Assistant Director of Appeals in a Tax Services Office of the Canada Revenue Agency and delivered or mailed to that office.
@ref Act s 27.2(2) (src:755-756)
GIVEN `the appeal is addressed to the Assistant Director of Appeals in a Tax Services Office of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is delivered to that office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is mailed to that office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27.2(2) — the appeal is addressed and sent as required` `the appeal is addressed to the Assistant Director of Appeals in a Tax Services Office of the Canada Revenue Agency` `the appeal is delivered to that office` `the appeal is mailed to that office` MEANS
        `the appeal is addressed to the Assistant Director of Appeals in a Tax Services Office of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    AND (`the appeal is delivered to that office` OR `the appeal is mailed to that office`)

-- src:757 | Decision
-- src:758 | (3) The Minister shall decide the appeal within a reasonable time after receiving it and shall notify the affected persons of the decision in any manner that the Minister considers adequate.
@ref Act s 27.2(3) (src:757-758)
GIVEN `the Minister decided the appeal within a reasonable time after receiving it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister notified the affected persons of the decision in a manner the Minister considers adequate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27.2(3) — the Minister has decided the appeal and notified the affected persons as required` `the Minister decided the appeal within a reasonable time after receiving it` `the Minister notified the affected persons of the decision in a manner the Minister considers adequate` MEANS
        `the Minister decided the appeal within a reasonable time after receiving it`
    AND `the Minister notified the affected persons of the decision in a manner the Minister considers adequate`

-- "Nothing in sections 26.1 to 27.2 restricts the authority of the Minister to make a decision under this Part on the
-- Minister's own initiative or to make an assessment after the date mentioned in subsection 26.1(2)". The rule says
-- whether sections 26.1 to 27.2 are a restriction in the case; it does not say the Minister may act, because other
-- provisions (such as the four-year limit in subsection 22(3)) may still restrict.
-- src:759 | Minister’s authority not restricted
-- src:760 | 27.3 Nothing in sections 26.1 to 27.2 restricts the authority of the Minister to make a decision under this Part on the Minister’s own initiative or to make an assessment after the date mentioned in subsection 26.1(2).
@ref Act s 27.3 (src:759-760)
GIVEN `the decision is made on the Minister's own initiative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessment is made after the date mentioned in subsection 26.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27.3 — sections 26.1 to 27.2 do not restrict the Minister's authority in the case` `the decision is made on the Minister's own initiative` `the assessment is made after the date mentioned in subsection 26.1(2)` MEANS
        `the decision is made on the Minister's own initiative`
    OR  `the assessment is made after the date mentioned in subsection 26.1(2)`

§§ `s 28 and 29 -- the Tax Court of Canada, finality and allowances`

-- (1.1): the time a decision "is communicated" is fixed by the rule, if any, made under paragraph 20(1.1)(h.1) of the
-- Tax Court of Canada Act. That Act is not deposited, so the day under the rule is a supplied fact (fork F16).
-- src:763 | Communication of decision
-- src:764 | (1.1) The determination of the time at which a decision on an appeal to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1 is communicated to a person shall be made in accordance with the rule, if any, made under paragraph 20(1.1)(h.1) of the Tax Court of Canada Act.
@ref Act s 28(1.1) (src:763-764)
GIVEN `the day fixed by the rule made under paragraph 20(1.1)(h.1) of the Tax Court of Canada Act, if there is such a rule` IS A MAYBE DATE -- out of range: that Act is not deposited
      `the day the decision is otherwise communicated to the person` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 28(1.1) — the day the decision on the appeal to the Minister is communicated to the person` `the day fixed by the rule made under paragraph 20(1.1)(h.1) of the Tax Court of Canada Act, if there is such a rule` `the day the decision is otherwise communicated to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day fixed by the rule made under paragraph 20(1.1)(h.1) of the Tax Court of Canada Act, if there is such a rule`
    WHEN JUST fixed THEN fixed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the decision is otherwise communicated to the person`

-- src:761 | Appeal to Tax Court of Canada
-- src:762 | 28 (1) A person affected by a decision on an appeal to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1, or the person’s representative, may, within 90 days after the decision is communicated to the person, or within any longer time that the Tax Court of Canada on application made to it within 90 days after the expiration of those 90 days allows, appeal from the decision to that Court in accordance with the Tax Court of Canada Act and the applicable rules of court made thereunder.
@ref Act s 28(1) (src:761-762)
GIVEN `the appellant is a person affected by the decision on the appeal to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant is the representative of a person affected by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the decision was communicated` IS A DATE
      `the day of the appeal to the Tax Court of Canada` IS A DATE
      `the Tax Court of Canada allowed a longer time, on an application made within 90 days after the expiration of the first 90 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer time the Court allowed, if it allowed one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(1) — the appeal to the Tax Court of Canada may be brought` `the appellant is a person affected by the decision on the appeal to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1` `the appellant is the representative of a person affected by the decision` `the day the decision was communicated` `the day of the appeal to the Tax Court of Canada` `the Tax Court of Canada allowed a longer time, on an application made within 90 days after the expiration of the first 90 days` `the last day of the longer time the Court allowed, if it allowed one` MEANS
        (`the appellant is a person affected by the decision on the appeal to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1` OR `the appellant is the representative of a person affected by the decision`)
    AND (    `a date is within a time limit after a start date`
                 `the day of the appeal to the Tax Court of Canada`
                 `the day the decision was communicated`
                 (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90)
         OR  (    `the Tax Court of Canada allowed a longer time, on an application made within 90 days after the expiration of the first 90 days`
              AND `the longer time the Court allowed covers the day of the appeal`))
    WHERE
        `the longer time the Court allowed covers the day of the appeal` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the last day of the longer time the Court allowed, if it allowed one`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST lastDay THEN `the day of the appeal to the Tax Court of Canada` AT MOST lastDay

@ref Act s 28(1) (src:761-762)
GIVEN `the day the decision was communicated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 28(1) — the last day for appealing to the Tax Court of Canada without more time` `the day the decision was communicated` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the day the decision was communicated` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90)

@ref Act s 28(1) (src:761-762)
GIVEN `the day the decision was communicated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 28(1) — the last day for applying to the Tax Court of Canada for a longer time` `the day the decision was communicated` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` (`the date a time limit ends` `the day the decision was communicated` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90)) (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90)

-- (1.2): section 167 of the Income Tax Act, "except paragraph 167(5)(a)", applies to applications under (1)
-- with such modifications as the circumstances require. That Act is not deposited (fork F10).
-- src:765 | Extension of time to appeal
-- src:766 | (1.2) Section 167, except paragraph 167(5)(a), of the Income Tax Act applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of applications made under subsection (1).
@ref Act s 28(1.2) (src:765-766)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection 28(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(1.2) — section 167 of the Income Tax Act, except paragraph 167(5)(a), applies to the application` `the application is made under subsection 28(1)` MEANS
    `the application is made under subsection 28(1)`

-- src:767 | Decision of Court
-- src:768 | (2) On an appeal under this section, the Tax Court of Canada may vacate, confirm or vary a decision on an appeal under section 27 or an assessment that is the subject of an appeal under section 27.1 or, in the case of an appeal under section 27.1, may refer the matter back to the Minister for reconsideration and reassessment, and shall without delay
-- src:769 | (a) notify the parties to the appeal in writing of its decision; and
-- src:770 | (b) give reasons for its decision, but, except where the Court deems it advisable in a particular case to give reasons in writing, the reasons given by it need not be in writing.
@ref Act s 28(2) (src:767-770)
DECLARE `cp2 Kind of appeal to the Tax Court of Canada` IS ONE OF
    `an appeal from a decision on an appeal to the Minister under section 27`
    `an appeal from an assessment that was the subject of an appeal to the Minister under section 27.1`

@ref Act s 28(2) (src:767-770)
DECLARE `cp2 Order of the Tax Court of Canada` IS ONE OF
    `vacate the decision or assessment`
    `confirm the decision or assessment`
    `vary the decision or assessment`
    `refer the matter back to the Minister for reconsideration and reassessment`

@ref Act s 28(2) (src:767-770)
GIVEN kind IS A `cp2 Kind of appeal to the Tax Court of Canada`
      order IS A `cp2 Order of the Tax Court of Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(2) — the Tax Court of Canada may make the order on the appeal` kind order MEANS
    IF order EQUALS `refer the matter back to the Minister for reconsideration and reassessment`
    THEN kind EQUALS `an appeal from an assessment that was the subject of an appeal to the Minister under section 27.1`
    ELSE TRUE

@ref Act s 28(2)(a) (src:767-770)
GIVEN `the Court has decided the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court notified the parties to the appeal in writing of its decision without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(2)(a) — the Court has notified the parties of its decision as required` `the Court has decided the appeal` `the Court notified the parties to the appeal in writing of its decision without delay` MEANS
        `the Court has decided the appeal`
    AND `the Court notified the parties to the appeal in writing of its decision without delay`

-- (b): the Court must give reasons; they need be in writing only where "the Court deems it advisable in a particular case".
@ref Act s 28(2)(b) (src:767-770)
GIVEN `the Court deems it advisable in the particular case to give reasons in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(2)(b) — the Court's reasons must be in writing` `the Court deems it advisable in the particular case to give reasons in writing` MEANS
    `the Court deems it advisable in the particular case to give reasons in writing`

-- src:771 | Authority to decide questions
-- src:772 | 29 (1) The authority of the Minister or the Tax Court of Canada to decide an appeal under section 27, 27.1 or 28 includes the authority to decide any question of fact or law necessary to be decided in the course of the appeal and to decide whether a person is or may be affected by the decision of the appeal.
@ref Act s 29(1) (src:771-772)
GIVEN `the appeal is under section 27, 27.1 or 28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is a question of fact or law necessary to be decided in the course of the appeal, or whether a person is or may be affected by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29(1) — the authority of the Minister or the Tax Court of Canada includes deciding the question` `the appeal is under section 27, 27.1 or 28` `the question is a question of fact or law necessary to be decided in the course of the appeal, or whether a person is or may be affected by the decision` MEANS
        `the appeal is under section 27, 27.1 or 28`
    AND `the question is a question of fact or law necessary to be decided in the course of the appeal, or whether a person is or may be affected by the decision`

-- (2): "Except as otherwise provided in this Act", the decision and the ruling are "final and binding for all purposes
-- of this Act". The Act itself provides an appeal from a ruling (section 27) and from the Minister's decision
-- (section 28), so finality is read as subject to an appeal that is still open (fork F15).
-- src:773 | Decisions and rulings final
-- src:774 | (2) Except as otherwise provided in this Act, the decision of the Minister or the Tax Court of Canada of an appeal under section 27, 27.1 or 28 and a ruling of an authorized officer under section 26.1 is final and binding for all purposes of this Act.
@ref Act s 29(2) (src:773-774)
GIVEN `the thing is a decision of the Minister or the Tax Court of Canada of an appeal under section 27, 27.1 or 28, or a ruling of an authorized officer under section 26.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act otherwise provides, for example by an appeal that is still open` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29(2) — the decision or ruling is final and binding for all purposes of this Act` `the thing is a decision of the Minister or the Tax Court of Canada of an appeal under section 27, 27.1 or 28, or a ruling of an authorized officer under section 26.1` `this Act otherwise provides, for example by an appeal that is still open` MEANS
        `the thing is a decision of the Minister or the Tax Court of Canada of an appeal under section 27, 27.1 or 28, or a ruling of an authorized officer under section 26.1`
    AND (NOT `this Act otherwise provides, for example by an appeal that is still open`)

-- src:775 | Allowance for attending appeal
-- src:776 | (3) If, on an appeal to the Tax Court of Canada from a decision of the Minister, a person affected by the decision is requested by the Court to attend before it on the consideration of the appeal and so attends, the person shall be paid such travel and other allowances, including compensation for loss of remunerative time, as are approved by the Treasury Board.
@ref Act s 29(3) (src:775-776)
GIVEN `the appeal to the Tax Court of Canada is from a decision of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person affected by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court requested the person to attend before it on the consideration of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person attended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29(3) — the person must be paid the travel and other allowances approved by the Treasury Board` `the appeal to the Tax Court of Canada is from a decision of the Minister` `the person is a person affected by the decision` `the Court requested the person to attend before it on the consideration of the appeal` `the person attended` MEANS
        `the appeal to the Tax Court of Canada is from a decision of the Minister`
    AND `the person is a person affected by the decision`
    AND `the Court requested the person to attend before it on the consideration of the appeal`
    AND `the person attended`

@ref Act s 29(3) (src:775-776)
GIVEN `the person must be paid the allowances under subsection 29(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the travel and other allowances approved by the Treasury Board, including compensation for loss of remunerative time` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: the Treasury Board's approval is not in any text deposited
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 29(3) — the allowances the person must be paid` `the person must be paid the allowances under subsection 29(3)` `the travel and other allowances approved by the Treasury Board, including compensation for loss of remunerative time` MEANS
    IF `the person must be paid the allowances under subsection 29(3)`
    THEN `the travel and other allowances approved by the Treasury Board, including compensation for loss of remunerative time`
    ELSE 0
